# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Strength-only boundary. This repo holds the engine and what builds, tests and
# benchmarks it. Everything below belongs to the workspace ABOVE this repo:
#   session notes / handoffs / briefs -> ../archive/engine-handoffs/<yyyy-mm>/
#   training pipeline and run output  -> ../training/
#   bench dumps and match results     -> ../results/
# `tests/repo_hygiene.rs` fails the build if any of it is tracked anyway.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Session notes: they describe a moment, the engine repo describes a program.
*HANDOFF*
*handoff*
MORNING_BRIEF*
SESSION_*
BRIEF_*
progress.txt

# Training scaffolding and its output.
/training/
/data/
*.jsonl
*.db
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.npz

# Bench and match dumps: numbers belong in ../results/ and in LEDGER.md.
